        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Jake White names Nathan Hughes, ex-England No. 8, for France clash",
          "body": "Fiji-born number eight Nathan Hughes, 35, won 22 caps for England between 2016 and 2019 and returns for Saturday's test against France in Lyon. Hughes qualifies under World Rugby's revised Regulation 8, which allows allegiance switches after a three-year absence from a previous national team with a birthright connection and World Rugby approval. He forms a loose trio with Pita-Gus Sowakula and Kitione Salawa, the second game of Jake White's tenure."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England's Tom Curry faces major injury fears before Australia Test",
          "body": "Springboks' Eben Etzebeth out of European tests with leg injury. Ireland's Caelan Doris and Jack Conan sidelined; Jansen starts."
        }
      ]
    },
    "386": {
