          "heading": "Steve Tandy defends naming record nine England-based players for Japan",
          "body": "Wales must embrace picking England-based players, Steve Tandy insists, after naming a record nine of them in the starting XV for Saturday's Nations Championship clash with Japan. \"Ultimately it doesn't matter where they play, it'll be the best players selected,\" said the Wales boss. He argues the players are in demand and performing well in those environments. Only six England-based players were in the 33-strong squad at the 2023 World Cup."
