          "kicker": "Pay dispute",
          "heading": "Rugby Australia sends pay offer directly to Wallabies, bypassing players' union",
          "body": "The pay talks are now being fought in public, with the governing body writing to players this week to spell out its terms. The letter went around the Rugby Union Players' Association, which handles negotiations. Rupa president Tom Robertson voiced disappointment at the timing, \"particularly while the Wallabies are on tour.\" RA chair Daniel Herbert said Rupa's counter-proposals \"threaten the future of the game in Australia.\" The previous agreement, struck in 2023, ran through the two Bledisloe Cup defeats to New Zealand."
